{"name":"Salty Dog","hex":"#234058","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salty dog","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An experienced sailor.","A sexually promiscuous man; a male sexual partner."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail consisting of gin or vodka, grapefruit juice, and a salt rim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salty_dog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salty dog (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"A salty dog is a cocktail made with gin or vodka and grapefruit juice, served in a highball glass with a salted rim. The salt distinguishes it from the related greyhound. It is traditionally made with gin and is believed to date back to the 1920s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Salty_Dog.jpg/330px-Salty_Dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salty_dog_(cocktail)"},{"title":"A Salty Dog","blocks":[{"text":"A Salty Dog is the third studio album by English rock band Procol Harum, released in 1969 by record labels Regal Zonophone and A&M."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/Procol_Harum-A_Salty_Dog_%28album_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Salty_Dog"},{"title":"Salty Dog (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Salty Dog was an American rock band from Los Angeles, formed in 1986 by former Max Havoc guitarist Scott Lane, bassist Michael Hannon, and drummer Khurt Maier who also played on Max Havoc's 1983 album. Later, they were joined by lead singer Jimmi Bleacher. The band was managed by Vicky Hamilton, who also managed Poison, Faster Pussycat, and Guns N' Roses."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salty_Dog_(band)"},{"title":"Dog","blocks":[{"text":"The dog is a domesticated descendant of wolves. Also called the domestic dog, it was selectively bred during the Late Pleistocene by hunter-gatherers. Dogs and the modern gray wolf share a common ancestor. Dogs were the first species to be domesticated over 14,000 years ago, before the development of agriculture, though genetic studies suggest the domestication process may have begun over 25,000 years ago. Due to their long association with humans, dogs have gained the ability to thrive on a starch-rich diet that would be inadequate for other canids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG/500px-Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG/1280px-Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG/500px-Dog_-_%E0%B4%A8%E0%B4%BE%E0%B4%AF-6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil